  "body": "## What changed\n\n`edit_machine` refuses a change from a non-turning machine to a lathe or mill-turn.\nThe refusal names `kind` and the machine model.\nIt tells the caller to load a turning machine file.\nThe refusal leaves the machine and command history unchanged.\nExisting turning machines still accept edits.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe declared kind overrides the kind inferred from the axes.\nThe edit previously accepted a lathe declaration on the Tormach 770MX without a work spindle.\nThe flattened machine data cannot prove a new turning capability.\nThe regression uses the top-level `kind` field from `get_job`.\nThe issue's nested `general.kind` form already fails as an unknown key.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `kind_edit_cannot_relabel_a_mill_for_turning` failed before the fix.\n  It checks document and setup machines, kind aliases, unchanged state, and undo history.\n- `an_existing_lathe_keeps_its_machine_edits` passes.\n- The mutation restored `upstream/main` source. The refusal pin failed again.\n  The fixed source was restored. All six `mcp_edit_machine` tests passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed all three steps.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n\nThe inherited sccache wrapper hung before compilation.\nThe checks ran with that optional wrapper disabled.\nThe decision is recorded in `docs/decisions/2602-machine-kind-kinematics.md`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The `.nc` and `.cl` diff is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical machine run or full release gate was performed.\nThe fix does not validate a full machine conversion.\nIt requires a turning machine file instead.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changed the implementation file or test file at the overlap check.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Refuse machine kind edits that enable turning on a non-turning machine.\n\nFixes #2602\n",
